# chela.env — the single source of truth for a chela install's config.
#
#   cp examples/chela.env ~/.chela/chela.env      # then edit
#
# Sourced by chela itself (chela/config.py, at import) and by scripts/run-chela.sh,
# which is what PM2/systemd should start. Nothing else should carry a copy of these
# values: a process manager's `env:` block is a second place for config to live, and a
# second place is where drift comes from. `chela doctor` compares the two and complains.
#
# An exported variable BEATS this file, so a one-off `CHELA_TMUX_SESSION=other chela
# status` still works. Every line here is optional — chela runs on documented defaults
# with an empty file, or with no file at all.
#
# NO SECRETS. Put TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and friends in ~/.chela/secrets.env (chmod 600);
# run-chela.sh sources that separately. This file is meant to be pasteable.

# The tmux session chela orchestrates. Default: chela.
CHELA_TMUX_SESSION=chela

# NOTE: CHELA_DIR is *not* set here. This file is FOUND via $CHELA_DIR, so it cannot
# move itself — export it in the environment (run-chela.sh does) if you want it
# somewhere other than ~/.chela. `chela doctor` errors if this file sets it anyway.

# Dashboard bind. The port is also what the Claude Code hooks plugin POSTs to, so it has
# to be the same number in every process — that is the whole reason this file exists.
# Prefer changing it here over `chela dashboard --port`, which is a per-process override
# that nothing else can see (the dashboard publishes what it really bound to
# $CHELA_DIR/dashboard.port so `chela plugin` stays right either way).
CHELA_DASH_HOST=127.0.0.1
CHELA_DASHBOARD_PORT=5001

# Embedded ttyd terminal wall. It serves writable shells: leave EXPOSE off unless the
# dashboard is behind a tailnet / SSH tunnel and you know what you are doing.
CHELA_TERMINALS_ENABLED=true
CHELA_TERMINALS_EXPOSE=false

# Window names to hide from discovery (placeholder / keep-alive windows), comma-separated.
# CHELA_IGNORE_WINDOWS=__main__

# Work-item dispatcher inside the daemon: colon-separated WORKFLOW.md paths.
#
# ⚠️ EMPTY DISABLES TWO THINGS, NOT ONE. Dispatch and reconciliation ride the SAME daemon
# tick, so an empty value means (a) no task is ever claimed from a tracker AND (b) no
# finished run is ever reconciled — a merged PR's run then sits in `awaiting_review`
# forever, holding a concurrency slot, so even a later fix stays blocked behind it. This
# variable once went missing from a live env file and the daemon ran for nine hours
# doing neither, in silence. It is spelled out here, and left in the file EMPTY rather
# than deleted, so the next person to read the file cannot fail to see it.
#
# Empty is a valid state — the `chela dispatch <workflow>` CLI still works, and the
# daemon now says "Work dispatcher: OFF" (WARNING) at startup, `chela doctor` WARNs, and
# the dashboard's Settings drawer shows it Off. Uncomment the second line to turn it on.
CHELA_DISPATCH_WORKFLOWS=
# CHELA_DISPATCH_WORKFLOWS=/path/to/repo/WORKFLOW.md

# Answering a gate from Telegram with ZERO keypresses (chela/gateanswer.py). When an
# agent asks an AskUserQuestion, its `PermissionRequest` hook is held open for up to this
# many seconds so you can tap the answer on your phone — the answer goes back through the
# hook, so no keystroke is ever sent to the pane (which is the ONLY safe way to answer a
# multi-question or multi-select picker).
#
# ⚠️ The agent is FROZEN while it waits, so the wait is bounded and it FAILS OPEN: when
# the budget runs out chela answers nothing, the picker is still on the pane, and the run
# is no worse off than before. It is never an auto-deny. 0 disables the hold entirely.
# The ceiling is the hook's own declared timeout (120s — Claude Code honours it verbatim,
# measured); a longer wait would be a wait that can never deliver, so it is clamped.
CHELA_GATE_WAIT_S=90

# How many gates may be held at once. Each one holds a dashboard request thread for its
# budget; past this bound the next gate is not held at all (it falls back to the pane).
CHELA_GATE_MAX_WAITS=8

# Phone push for "N commits behind — run chela update" and needs-input pings (ntfy).
# ⚠️ PER-INSTALL — pick your OWN topic; do NOT copy another machine's. ntfy.sh topics are
# UNAUTHENTICATED (anyone who knows the name can read AND publish), so a shared topic means
# your pings land on their phone and they can read yours. Leave empty to disable.
CHELA_NOTIFY_URL=

# Session-sharing relay (chela/collab-relay, a Cloudflare Worker). Empty = sharing off.
# This one is MEANT to be shared: two installs that want to share terminals point at the
# SAME relay. Run your own (`cd chela/collab-relay && npm run deploy`) and use its wss:// URL.
CHELA_COLLAB_RELAY=
